 &nbsp; 
 
 Emptying out the notebook as we head into the weekend... 

 🎓 Academia: Harvard University yesterday released its annual financial report , and it was the mixed bag one might imagine.

 Plus side: The world's largest endowment generated a 27.1% return, easily besting the S&amp;P 500 and rising to nearly $68 billion. Venture capital played a key role, perhaps validating a Yale Model that had been falling out of favor . Minus side: Most endowment monies are restricted — i.e., can't be used for general purposes — and Harvard has been under relentless attack by the Trump administration (research grant freezes, international student bans, large endowment tax, etc.). In fact, a spokesperson tells me that ongoing and one-time legal fees totaled around $210 million during the fiscal year. To make budgets work, the university has had to do layoffs and keep some other roles unfilled. Irony side: One of the people responsible for helping Harvard keep its financial equilibrium might be Trump pal Elon Musk, as the school recently disclosed a multibillion-dollar investment in SpaceX. 🗓️ IPO calendar: Anthropic still appears to be on track to go public in 2026, having just shared Q3 financials with prospective investors, but time is a'ticking.

 Let's assume that it wants to price before Thanksgiving week and that it plans to match SpaceX's lightning-fast speed (16 biz days between the S-1 flip and listing). That gives Anthropic a flip deadline of Oct. 29 or 30, depending on how you view Veterans Day. But next week feels more likely, to build in a bit of cushion. In the meantime, what do we think the ticker symbol will be? I've seen a bunch of "DOOM" suggestions on social media, but an even more flippant one might be "SAMA." 💊 Magic wand: AI drug developer Iambic Therapeutics closed its first day of trading up more than 18%, and I spoke briefly with CEO Tom Miller.

 He emphasized that the company's lead oncology drug has been administered to more than 100 patients, rather than just being simulated in models, and said he views the VC valuation for Isomorphic as validation for Iambic's growth story. I also asked him about the recent claim that some AI researchers have taken up smoking to signal their faith in the technology's ability to cure cancer. Miller looked a bit shocked, and then replied: "I think it's important to not regard AI as a magic wand. And Iambic has never pitched ourselves as an AI magic wand." ❓ Quiz time: Can you name the family office manager who just spun out and raised an independent fund? Hint: The family in question has more than one family office.

 🎲 Where in the world: Flying out to Vegas on Sunday for a brief stop at Money 2020. Hope to see some of you there... 

 
 
